- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/uvtopolar.html
- Summary (EN): Converts the Cartesian (x, y) position of each pixel into polar coordinates: its distance from an origin and its angle. It changes each pixel's coordinate values in place and does not move pixels. To relocate pixels, the page recommends a UV Map, then this node, then a UV Sample.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud convertit les coordonnées cartésiennes UV en coordonnées polaires, angle et distance à l'origine, sans déplacer les pixels.

- Inputs meaning: ["uv: UV layer or attribute containing the Cartesian coordinates to convert."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "The layer type the source accepts. Details are in the Signatures glossary entry."}, {"name": "Angle Units", "meaning": "Circles (2pi) gives complete rotations from 0 to 1, and is the default. Radians is the unit circle distance used by VEX and OpenCL. Degrees is the human-readable format used by expressions."}, {"name": "Output angle", "meaning": "Mono layer or attribute with the rotation of each point about the origin."}, {"name": "Output length", "meaning": "Mono layer or attribute with each point's distance from the origin."}]

- Caveats: ["The page does not say how the origin itself is handled, where the zero angle lies, or which direction is positive.", "The Signature parameter is described only by a reference to the glossary.", "The node does not resample or reposition pixels. Use the UV Map and UV Sample workflow for that."]

